win32u: keep the driver's placement for single-mode display sources

Wayland outputs expose one host mode. add_modes() then takes the physical
mode from the host mode list, which carries no position, and the first
current mode from that physical mode. Every source therefore lands on the
origin: on a two-output desktop both monitors overlap at (0,0), the work area
of the second is clipped to an empty strip, and a window assigned to it is
placed outside the desktop window. Hit testing fails there, so the owner
process never delivers WebView frames and Desktop stays blank.
Carry the driver's current position into the physical mode, as the
multi-mode path already does, and follow the host placement while no
emulated mode is active.
The second hunk applies to every driver: a stored current mode of the
physical size takes the host's position, so a position-only change that an
application requested for a single-mode source is not kept. A Wayland client
cannot move an output in any case.
Wine-derived change: LGPL-2.1-or-later.

--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -2218,6 +2218,13 @@
     }
 
     physical = modes_count == 1 ? *modes : *current;
+    /* Host mode lists carry no placement. Keep the driver's position for a
+     * single-mode source, as the multi-mode path already does. */
+    if (current->dmFields & DM_POSITION)
+    {
+        physical.dmFields |= DM_POSITION;
+        physical.dmPosition = current->dmPosition;
+    }
     if (ctx->is_primary) ctx->primary = *current;
 
     detached.dmPelsWidth = 0;
@@ -2233,6 +2240,13 @@
     {
         if (!read_source_mode( source->key, ENUM_CURRENT_SETTINGS, &virtual ) || is_detached_mode( &virtual ))
             virtual = physical;
+        else if ((physical.dmFields & DM_POSITION) && virtual.dmPelsWidth == physical.dmPelsWidth &&
+                 virtual.dmPelsHeight == physical.dmPelsHeight)
+        {
+            /* No emulated mode is active: follow the host placement. */
+            virtual.dmFields |= DM_POSITION;
+            virtual.dmPosition = physical.dmPosition;
+        }
 
         if ((virtual_modes = get_virtual_modes( current, &physical, host_modes, host_modes_count, &virtual_count )))
         {
